elle (docs): Heads-up — I'm going to split the big troubleshooting runbook (rate-limit/timeouts/context limits) into two pages: a quick mitigation checklist and a deep-dive troubleshooting guide. Want to land the structure + update any example snippets that will move.

sam (eng-runtime): +1. Can we add a tiny JS SDK snippet that trims context client-side before retrying? Current examples are mostly Python.

taylor (devex): I can write the JS snippet. Recommended backoff: jittered exp backoff starting ~200ms, cap ~5s, max 6 retries for non-streaming idempotent calls. Does that match docs tone?

mike (eng-sre): Sounds fine. Also found two broken links in the private deploy section that point to old internal anchors — will add them to the link-fix list. We should prefer stable permalinks and add a redirect from the old 429 section.

elle (docs): Good. Proposed division: quick-mitigation.md (one-page checklist + copy-paste snippets) and troubleshooting-deep-dive.md (logs, reproduce steps, SRE playbook). Assign snippet authors and add redirects.

sam (eng-runtime): I'll review the JS snippet and add a small server-side pseudocode for cache invalidation + retry semantics so folks know when to rely on prefix caching vs trimming.

taylor (devex): Draft JS snippet below, will open PR against docs/runbooks/quick-mitigation. Feel free to nit: 
```js
// trim last messages to fit context limit, then retry with backoff
async function callWithTrimAndRetry(client, prompt, maxTokens) {
  let attempts = 0;
  let backoff = 200; // ms
  while (attempts < 6) {
    try {
      return await client.generate({ prompt });
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.code === 429) {
        // trim oldest messages to free tokens, then retry after backoff + jitter
        prompt = trimOldestMessages(prompt, maxTokens);
        await sleep(backoff + Math.floor(Math.random() * 100));
        backoff = Math.min(backoff * 2, 5000);
        attempts += 1;
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('Retries exhausted');
}
```

mike (eng-sre): Nice — add a note: don't retry non-idempotent actions silently. Recommend tagging retried requests (X-Retry: true) for tracing. Also add snippet showing how to fall back to a cheaper/shorter model variant if retries fail.

sam (eng-runtime): Agree re: model fallback. I'll add a small YAML example for routing policy + a one-liner to enable auto-fallback in Dedicated configs.

elle (docs): Action items: taylor -> open PR with JS snippet + checklist (assign devex reviewer) by EOD Thu; sam -> YAML fallback example + review; mike -> list of broken links & KMS stub 404; elle -> redirects and runbook split + create meta-index page. I'll tag reviewers in the PRs.

